26
00:01:02.410 --> 00:01:04.840 line:15%
Well, I would say what worries me most

27
00:01:04.840 --> 00:01:06.140 line:15%
or possibly scares me

28
00:01:06.140 --> 00:01:11.140 line:15%
is if a man hasn't been completely honest on his profile

29
00:01:11.610 --> 00:01:15.200 line:15%
and of course the guy that's too aggressive.

30
00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:18.160
Damona, what are your general tips

31
00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:21.980
for those particular anxieties or first dates in general?

32
00:01:21.980 --> 00:01:23.700
Well, I do wanna acknowledge

33
00:01:23.700 --> 00:01:25.520
those things are definite red flags,

34
00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:27.410
so you gotta look out for those.

35
00:01:27.410 --> 00:01:30.800
Those things that make you feel uncomfortable,

36
00:01:30.800 --> 00:01:34.840
that's always your first thing to guide you

37
00:01:34.840 --> 00:01:35.850
through the date.

38
00:01:35.850 --> 00:01:39.000
I want you to also prepare for the dates a little bit,

39
00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:42.190
and to remember how important body language is.

40
00:01:42.190 --> 00:01:44.700
So don't be afraid, you got this new body,

41
00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:46.950 line:15%
you lost 120 pounds.

42
00:01:46.950 --> 00:01:48.922 line:15%
That's amazing, amazing.
Thank you.

43
00:01:48.922 --> 00:01:49.758 line:15%
(audience cheers)

44
00:01:49.758 --> 00:01:51.093 line:15%
You look so beautiful.

45
00:01:51.093 --> 00:01:53.620 line:15%
Thank you.
Yeah.

46
00:01:53.620 --> 00:01:56.178 line:15%
So live in your body, use it, use your body language.

47
00:01:56.178 --> 00:01:58.650 line:15%
And then you've gotta prepare for the date.

48
00:01:58.650 --> 00:02:01.170 line:15%
So I want you, I'm gonna give you a little homework,

49
00:02:01.170 --> 00:02:04.490 line:15%
I want you to create a curiosity list

50
00:02:04.490 --> 00:02:05.850 line:15%
the next time that you have a date,

51
00:02:05.850 --> 00:02:08.420 line:15%
things that you're just curious to know about them.

52
00:02:08.420 --> 00:02:12.060 line:15%
And also prepare for the questions you will inevitably get,

53
00:02:12.060 --> 00:02:15.130 line:15%
which are, what do you like to do for fun?

54
00:02:15.130 --> 00:02:17.340 line:15%
What are you looking for?

55
00:02:17.340 --> 00:02:18.800 line:15%
Why are you divorced?

56
00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:21.060 line:15%
Which you are not obligated to answer.

57
00:02:21.060 --> 00:02:24.830 line:15%
So have a coy, fun comment at the ready

58
00:02:24.830 --> 00:02:26.920 line:15%
when you get that question, 'cause you inevitably will.

59
00:02:26.920 --> 00:02:29.040
And then, what do you think the ideal length

60
00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:30.490
of a first date is?

61
00:02:30.490 --> 00:02:32.130 line:15%
Well, actually, that is one of my questions,

62
00:02:32.130 --> 00:02:34.850 line:15%
how long should a first date last?

63
00:02:34.850 --> 00:02:36.010 line:15%
About an hour.

64
00:02:36.010 --> 00:02:37.780
And I want you to think of it like this.

65
00:02:37.780 --> 00:02:39.580
You want the energy to feel like

66
00:02:39.580 --> 00:02:42.890
it is ending on a high point, it's ending in the middle.

67
00:02:42.890 --> 00:02:46.600
So most people will remember the beginning of a date

68
00:02:46.600 --> 00:02:48.140
and the end of a date.

69
00:02:48.140 --> 00:02:51.330
But if the end of the date is like, we went for three hours,

70
00:02:51.330 --> 00:02:54.110
we had dinner, we ran out of things to talk about,

71
00:02:54.110 --> 00:02:57.530
that's what you'll remember, and that's what he'll remember.

72
00:02:57.530 --> 00:02:59.420
So even if you're having a great time,

73
00:02:59.420 --> 00:03:00.760
I know it's very hard,

74
00:03:00.760 --> 00:03:02.810
we have to just hold back a little bit,

75
00:03:02.810 --> 00:03:05.290
and end the date feeling like it's in the middle,

76
00:03:05.290 --> 00:03:07.895
and you'll probably get an invitation for the next one.

77
00:03:07.895 --> 00:03:11.675
(audience applauds)

78
00:03:11.675 --> 00:03:14.430
Rachael, I think you have another question.

79
00:03:14.430 --> 00:03:16.900
Last question for Damona, I'd love for you to ask.

80
00:03:16.900 --> 00:03:17.930
Oh yes, I do.

81
00:03:17.930 --> 00:03:20.640 line:15%
Now, if there is no chemistry

82
00:03:20.640 --> 00:03:22.550 line:15%
and the guy is quite a gentleman,

83
00:03:22.550 --> 00:03:24.500 line:15%
should I go on a second date?

84
00:03:24.500 --> 00:03:26.210 line:15%
Oh yeah, why not?

85
00:03:26.210 --> 00:03:27.043
Why not?

86
00:03:27.043 --> 00:03:28.040
I mean, on a first date,

87
00:03:28.040 --> 00:03:30.950
most people are not really themselves anyway.

88
00:03:30.950 --> 00:03:34.330
If you're still curious by the end of the first date

89
00:03:34.330 --> 00:03:36.730
to know more about him, go on the second date.

90
00:03:36.730 --> 00:03:39.150
If you're still curious by the end of the second date,

91
00:03:39.150 --> 00:03:39.983
go on a third.

92
00:03:39.983 --> 00:03:41.610
I have a three date rule.

93
00:03:41.610 --> 00:03:43.430
If by the end of the third date,

94
00:03:43.430 --> 00:03:46.190
you're not feeling anything, then you can let it go,

95
00:03:46.190 --> 00:03:49.302
but you've given it your best shot.

96
00:03:49.302 --> 00:03:52.310
To remember this, I'll give you a little phrase.

97
00:03:52.310 --> 00:03:54.270
Drew loves my little zingers.

98
00:03:54.270 --> 00:03:58.320
Sparks in three or let it be. (laughs)

99
00:03:58.320 --> 00:04:00.390
I like that.
That'll keep you motivated.

100
00:04:00.390 --> 00:04:02.839
Sparks in three or let it be.

101
00:04:02.839 --> 00:04:04.100
(Damona laughs)

102
00:04:04.100 --> 00:04:06.267
Rachael, how does this feel?

103
00:04:06.267 --> 00:04:09.630
Great, I really appreciate your advice very much.

104
00:04:09.630 --> 00:04:11.458
It's my pleasure, I'm here to help.

105
00:04:11.458 --> 00:04:14.625 line:15%
(upbeat bright music)

